NAME
       play - play an audio file or a tone

SYNOPSIS
       play file.wav | file.mp3
       play -t [freq] [secs]

DESCRIPTION
       Plays a RIFF/WAVE or MPEG audio file through whichever driver
       claimed the sound card. Samples are converted to 16-bit stereo
       for the device.

       A file whose contents are not MPEG audio is reported with the
       container that was actually found, so an .mp3 name on an MP4 or
       Ogg file is named as such rather than blamed on the decoder.

OPTIONS
       -t, --tone [F] [S]   play a triangle tone of F Hz for S seconds
                            (default 440 Hz for 2 s)

EXAMPLES
       play /usr/share/media/Maxx-Get-A-Way.mp3
       play -t 440 2

SEE ALSO
       mixer(1)
